        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "634f2f99-117d-5629-aba9-1ff5ec210135",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Frank Ellis Boynton, Charles Lawrence Boynton, Chauncey Beadle, George Vanderbilt\n- Organizations: Biltmore Estate\n- Places: Asheville, North Carolina, Southeastern United States\n- Roles: American botanist\n- Topics: Gilded Age\n\nFacts:\n- Frank Ellis Boynton was born on July 10, 1859, and was a self-taught American botanist active in the Southeastern United States.\n- Frank Ellis Boynton worked at Biltmore Estate with his brother, Charles Lawrence Boynton, and Chauncey Beadle.\n- Biltmore Estate is a 6,950.4-acre private estate and tourist attraction near Asheville, North Carolina.\n- Biltmore Estate is still owned by George Vanderbilt's descendants.\n- Biltmore Estate stands as one of the most prominent remaining examples of the Gilded Age.\n- Frank Ellis Boynton died on December 10, 1942.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
